+Make the zechusim COMPOUND — the board should feel like one growing collective zechus,
+
+not isolated pledges. Combine three layers:
+
+
+
+A. FRAMING: Add a headline binding all pledges, e.g. "Together, the kehillah is keeping
+
+[total] extra minutes of Shabbos — a collective zechus for all [N] names." Every new
+
+pledge visibly grows this shared total.
+
+
+
+C. FULL COMPOUNDING: Treat all active tosfos as one collective zechus applied to EVERY
+
+name on the board:
+
+- When someone pledges (dedicating primarily to one name), their tosfos also counts toward
+
+  every other name's zechus — joining one joins all.
+
+- Each name's card reflects the whole kehillah standing with it: show it's held b'zchus by
+
+  the full community (total minutes + N people), alongside its own pledgers.
+
+- The Mi Shebeirach / names card can note the tefillah is b'zchus all the names together.
+
+Tell me your data-model approach and send any migration SQL (likely a display-layer change
+
+or a small flag — no rewrite of existing rows).
+
+
+
+D. VISUAL CHAIN: Render the pledges as a growing line of candles where each new one lights
+
+the next — subtle momentum, "rolling off each one." Honor prefers-reduced-motion (static).
+
+
+
+Keep it tasteful and on-theme. Commit + deploy; I'll verify live.
+

